# Copy to /opt/tijarah/.env on the server, fill in, then: chmod 600 .env
#
# This file is the entire trust anchor of the installation. AUTH_SECRET both
# signs the login sessions AND derives the key that encrypts the Fast Hub and
# Salla credentials in the database (src/lib/crypto.ts). Losing it locks you
# out of those credentials; leaking it hands them over.

# Absolute, not relative. A relative "file:./dev.db" resolves against the
# process's working directory, which is not always what you expect under
# systemd — and the wrong answer is a SECOND, empty database that looks like
# the app lost all your data.
DATABASE_URL="file:/opt/tijarah/data/app.db"

# Generate ON THE SERVER, never reuse the laptop's:
#   openssl rand -base64 48
#
# If you change this AFTER the database already holds Fast Hub or Salla
# credentials, those rows become unreadable (CRYPTO_UNREADABLE) and must be
# re-entered on the settings screens. Everything else — products, stock,
# costs, orders, the login password — is unaffected.
AUTH_SECRET=""

# The public address, with scheme and no trailing slash. Salla compares its
# OAuth redirect against this CHARACTER FOR CHARACTER, so it must match the
# Callback URL registered in the Salla Partners portal exactly:
#   https://tijarahsmart.com/api/salla/callback
APP_URL="https://tijarahsmart.com"
